{title: 320 - Lord of Creation}
{artist: Seventh-day Adventist Hymnal}
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: Eb}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{tag: Gospel}
{tag: }

Verse 1:
[Eb]Lord of creation, [Bb]to [Eb/G]you [Cm]be [Eb]all praise!
[Bb]Most mighty your [Eb]working, [Cm]most [Bb/D]wondrous your ways!
[Ab]Your glory and might [Eb]are beyond [Cm]us [Bb]to [Ab]tell,
[Eb/G]And yet [Bb/D]in [Cm]the heart of [Eb/G]the humble [Ab]you dwell.

Verse 2:
[Eb]Lord of all power, [Ab]I [Eb/G]give [Bb]you [Eb]my will,
[Bb]In joyful obedience [Cm]your [Bb/D]tasks [Eb]to [Bb]fulfill.
[Ab]Your bondage is freedom; [Eb]your [Bb/D]service is [Ab]song;
[Eb/G]And held [Bb/D]in [Cm]your keeping, [Eb/G]my weakness [Ab]is strong.

Verse 3:
[Eb]Lord of all wisdom, [Ab]I [Eb/G]give [Bb]you [Eb]my mind,
[Bb]Rich truth [Fm]that [Bb/D]surpasses [Cm]man's [Bb/D]knowledge to find;
[Ab]What eye has not seen and [Eb]what [Bb/D]ear [Cm]has [Bb]not [Ab]heard
[Eb/G]Is taught [Bb/D]by [Cm]your spirit [Eb/G]and shines [Ab]from your [Eb]word.

Verse 4:
[Eb]Lord of all [Ab]being, [Bb]I [Eb/G]give [Cm]you [Eb]my all,
[Bb]If I ever disown you, [Cm]I [Bb/D]stumble and fall;
[Ab]But led in your service [Eb]your [Bb/D]word [Cm]to [Bb]obey,
[Eb/G]I'll walk [Bb/D]in [Cm]your freedom [Eb/G]to the [Fm/Ab]end [Ab]of the [Eb]way.
